# Machine — the general conformance machine

The library root. The design basis is `MACHINE-ALGEBRA.md` beside this file
(pre-grade until grilled — ruling CV-4); no definition enters this library
before its slice of the algebra ratifies (estate C4). Slices arrive as
`Machine/<Slice>.lean` modules, each against a grilled section of the
algebra, each carrying its obligations from the §8 table.

House reuse rule: the experimental trees (`experiments/entity-store-*`)
are the worked instance — reuse their patterns (gates, obligation ledgers,
framed encodings, decidable admission) rather than re-deriving them.
Style reference: Functional Programming in Lean
(https://lean-lang.org/functional_programming_in_lean/).
